    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0455" n="443" xml:id="pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/2543: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-19T14:00:00-03:00">April 19, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>331. For the Under Secretary. Department’s telegram No. 166, April 3, 6 p.m.
                    Aranha says that after much consideration he has come to the conclusion that it
                    would be unwise to send European refugees to the Amazon region. “They would
                    never remain there,” said he, “and we would have endless difficulties with
                    them.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
